body: "## Hosted failure plus exact static evidence\nAt PR #36 head `c6fa42c8db6e671a7166ea16672154ec97153e80`, both current hosted Node jobs fail the behavioral-revert gate:\n- [Node 22](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40508362808/job/122218898056)\n- [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40508362808/job/122218898530)\n\n`fatal child evidence mutation boundary: expected 1 exact fixed snippet match(es)` reports `0 !== 1` from `test/revert-source.ts:9`, invoked by `test/revert.ts:75` in the shallow-clone gate. Node22 reports 411 tests,409 passing,2 failed (the subtest and containing parent).\n\nThe exact `before` string in [test/revert.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/c6fa42c8db6e671a7166ea16672154ec97153e80/test/revert.ts) still expects `await this.client.comments(...)`. The current [src/ledger.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/c6fa42c8db6e671a7166ea16672154ec97153e80/src/ledger.ts) wraps that operation in `await this.mutate(() => this.client.comments(...))`. A static literal-count oracle independently confirms zero target matches versus the required one. No local crash/revert/provider execution was needed or performed.\n\n## Expected / impact\nThe fatal-child evidence proof must still remove its intended mutation/error-boundary invariant, execute the targeted regression, and establish an assertion failure for the intended reason before restoring source bytes. Currently it aborts while locating the stale snippet, so the intended behavioral proof is not run and normal release checks fail.\n\nThis is distinct from #37's total retry-budget overrun and upstream pm-cli#1609's dead-owner recovery semantics; these logs do not establish another dead-owner timeout. The current [accepted tracker record](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/c6fa42c8db6e671a7166ea16672154ec97153e80/.agents/pm/issues/pm-rlm-sdk-dead-fence.toon) requires preserving crash-safety assertions while implementing bounded retry behavior.\n\n## Acceptance / regression\n- Update the mutation target to the current retry-wrapped source without removing the fatal-child evidence assertion.\n- Assert exactly one replacement and verify the intended targeted regression fails for the removed invariant, not fixture/snippet setup.\n- Restore source byte-for-byte and keep complete shallow-clone/revert gates green on the final head for Node22/26.\n- Do not weaken coverage, skip the proof, or treat ordinary branch coverage as equivalent behavioral evidence.\n\nAll37 all-status issue/PR records, current PR conversation/inline/reviews and the accepted tracker record were checked; no existing issue owns this stale-target gate failure. Full package certification remains incomplete.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-27T19:17:00Z)\n>\n> ### Additional current-head behavioral-proof evidence\n> \n> This is a related proof-maintenance gap in PR #39, distinct from the original fatal-child target in PR #36.\n> \n> At `f0df94bd93a2abb24681398ad90cb256b42e9309`, the native SDK compare-and-set proof in [test/reconcile-revert.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/f0df94bd93a2abb24681398ad90cb256b42e9309/test/reconcile-revert.ts#L16) expects the exact snippet `match: { key: 'rlm_state', value: expected }, `. The new [history-fenced ledger writer](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/f0df94bd93a2abb24681398ad90cb256b42e9309/src/ledger.ts) no longer contains it. An independent exact-source count found zero matches, agreeing with the hosted expected-one/actual-zero failure. This establishes a stale proof target and missing regression evidence, not failure of the new history fence.\n> \n> The current [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40557881142/job/122378707617) and [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40557881142/job/122378706947) also fail the ledger-storage-revert lease-free hydration proof during its induced regression fixture with `Run checkpoint is invalid`, rather than the qualifying expected assertion. That intentionally modified copy is not evidence of production checkpoint corruption.\n> \n> Node 22 reports 448/451 tests passing. Node 26 reports 447/451, including the separately tracked dead-writer recovery failure under upstream pm-cli #1609. Counts include parent/subtest failures, not three or four independent runtime defects. Keep that recovery gap separate from these proof targets.\n> \n> The [accepted repair-runs record](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/f0df94bd93a2abb24681398ad90cb256b42e9309/.agents/pm/features/pm-rlm-repair-runs.toon) retains unchanged 100% gates and actual behavioral-revert qualification.\n> \n> Acceptance:\n> - Retarget the proof to the authoritative history/SDK compare-and-set boundary.\n> - Demonstrate fixed passes, intentional regression fails by the intended assertion (not setup, parsing or refusal mismatch), and restored source passes.\n> - Repair the lease-free regression proof without weakening validation or accepting an unrelated error as success.\n> - Re-run the exact revised-head Node 22/26 and npm/Bun gates, retaining the separate dead-writer recovery limitation.\n> \n> Limits: exact-source static predicate plus hosted logs; no local crash, concurrency or provider reproduction. Public repair-contract modules independently passed 14 schema/topology/accounting assertions under Node 24.22.1, which does not certify repair execution or the whole package. All 39 issue/PR records and current PR discussion/reviews were checked before adding this evidence to the existing proof-maintenance owner. No implementation or configuration changes were made.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-27T20:41:57Z)\n>\n> ### Latest-head reconciliation: two earlier proof failures fixed, a different proof still does not qualify\n> \n> At PR #39 head `90e7fae6549909f0bc96229f1532c9edbf6c2386`, the prior comment's native SDK compare-and-set target and lease-free hydration proof now pass in the hosted logs. Do not continue reporting those two old failures as current.\n> \n> The remaining `reconcile-revert.ts` failure is the **completion uses durable counters** proof. Its exact source transform replaces `const state = await this.load(snapshot.run);` with `const state = snapshot;`. The targeted test deliberately reopens the native item after loading its snapshot, then invokes completion. In the intentionally regressed copy, the retained history guard refuses that stale snapshot with `RlmError`, code `busy`, message `Checkpoint history advanced; reload inside the run lease`. The proof helper requires an assertion failure; this typed refusal does not establish the intended wrong-answer/counter assertion and the proof gate fails.\n> \n> Sources:\n> - [Exact proof target](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90e7fae6549909f0bc96229f1532c9edbf6c2386/test/reconcile-revert.ts#L17)\n> - [Completion regression fixture](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90e7fae6549909f0bc96229f1532c9edbf6c2386/test/checkpoint-concurrency.test.ts#L134-L158)\n> - [Authoritative reload and history guard](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90e7fae6549909f0bc96229f1532c9edbf6c2386/src/ledger.ts#L183-L225)\n> - [Node 22 current-head job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40576360315/job/122443739088): 461/463 passing, including the failing proof subtest and its containing parent.\n> - [Node 26 current-head job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40576360315/job/122443739578): 460/463 passing, including the separately tracked root-write/dead-writer failure under upstream pm-cli #1609.\n> \n> This is a changed behavioral-proof qualification gap, **not evidence that production code emits stale answers or corrupts checkpoints**. The retained history guard is doing useful fail-closed work. Eight independent exact-source assertions confirm the current replacement target, fixture ordering and guard/qualification conditions; no local crash, concurrent writer, provider or production mutation was run.\n> \n> Acceptance:\n> - Preserve the authoritative reload and history fencing; do not weaken the safety guard merely to make the proof pass.\n> - Make the proof demonstrate its declared invariant using a fixture/transform that fails for that intended reason, or explicitly test the intended typed-refusal regression contract with equally strong fixed/reverted/restored evidence.\n> - Keep the ordinary fixed-code test passing, restore source bytes exactly, and pass complete shallow-clone/revert gates on Node 22/26 at the final head.\n> - Retain the separate #1609 recovery limitation and unchanged coverage thresholds.\n> \n> All 39 all-status issue/PR records, the existing issue's comments and current PR conversation were checked. This is new evidence for the existing proof-maintenance owner, not a new issue. The source change also adds native ownership/unreachable-graph refusal and uses shared SDK lock recovery; full repair execution, concurrency and backend conformance remain outside this bounded check.\n>"
